{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the day HaShem spoke to Moses.</b> When HaShem spoke to Moses to speak to Pharaoh, and he replied that they would not listen to him — behold, after He commanded him and Aaron to act as officers over Israel and over Pharaoh, as He mentioned, Scripture clarifies that their designation was not equal, but rather that Moses would be elohim to Pharaoh, and Aaron would serve him as translator and interpreter."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:39.944674509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}